{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01P2iaodw1WCXuHREBfDqMrn","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me think about how to use Java Streams here.\n\nThe DP loop structure is:\n```\nfor len in 2..n:\n  for i in 0..n-len:\n    j = i + len\n    cost[i][j] = min over k in i+1..j of (cost[i][k] + cost[k][j] + dims[i]*dims[k]*dims[j])\n```\n\nThe outer two loops (len, i) can potentially be streamed, but the key constraint is that the inner computation depends on previously computed values (dynamic programming). The order of computation must be preserved — specifically, `len` must be processed in order (2, 3, ..., n-1) because a subproblem of length `len` depends on subproblems of shorter lengths.\nThe inner loop over `k` is a perfect fit for streams since it's just finding the minimum cost across all split points. I can use `IntStream` to iterate over the range of possible split positions and apply a comparator to find the optimal one. For the outer loops, I need to maintain sequential ordering for `len`, so I'll use `IntStream.range` with `forEach` to keep the stream syntax while respecting the dependency order, then apply the stream-based reduction for the innermost loop. Completing the stream-based approach...\n\nThe `forEach()` loops handle the nested iterations, while the inner `min()` operation with a comparator finds the optimal split point — `orElseThrow()` is safe since there's always at least one valid `k` when `len >= 2`. For the `Result` record, I'm defining it as an immutable value type with auto-generated accessors and equality methods, though the mutable array contents mean it won't be deeply immutable.\n\nRecords nested in interfaces are implicitly `public static` as of Java 16+. The key difference is that record fields become accessor methods — so `result.minCost` becomes `result.minCost()` and `result.splitTable` becomes `result.splitTable()`. I need to update the calls in `MatrixChainMultiplication.run()` to use the method syntax instead of field access.\n\nUpdating the interface and implementation files...","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":896,"cache_read_input_tokens":40277,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":896},"output_tokens":25,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b970ed32-32ea-4b00-a548-971f212b94a0","uuid":"78864899-b162-45b5-971c-12be836a1c28","request_id":"req_011CcjvHcuEdKW4JvCBcMeQV"}
